<title>USA: American White Cross delisted from Nasdaq.</title>
<headline>American White Cross delisted from Nasdaq.</headline>
<dateline>DAYVILLE, Conn. 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>American White Cross Inc, which filed for bankruptcy reorganization last month, said Wednesday that its shares are no longer trading on the Nasdaq.</p>
<p>The company said the delisting was the result of its failure to meet certain listing requirements of the Nasdaq SmallCap Market.</p>
<p>American White Cross manufactures and markets a wide variety of health and personal care products.</p>
<p>	  ((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
